(6890023, 1037664, 61396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Alexkc:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tanguera:</b></div><hr/><i> Excellent idea, beautifully styled, but there''s just not enough separation between the subject and bg. On my screen it looks like a disembodied face and hand </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the comment Johanna  :)<br/> <br/>On my monitor (and after printing) I can say that separation between backgroung and subject is enough, but it can surely be perceived as a thin line :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>on some monitors viewing angle can make quite a difference, especially with dark tones (see more at <a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viewing_angle" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viewing_angle</a>).<br/>In any case, an excellent job as usual, Alessandro.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Alexkc: Originally posted by tanguera: Excellent idea, beautifully styled, but there''s just not enough separation between the subject and bg. On my screen it looks like a disembodied face and hand   Thanks for the comment Johanna  :) On my monitor (and after printing) I can say that separation between backgroung and subject is enough, but it can surely be perceived as a thin line :)  on some monitors viewing angle can make quite a difference, especially with dark tones (see more at //en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viewing_angle).In any case, an excellent job as usual, Alessandro.', '2012-10-24 11:33:53.000000', NULL, 0),
