(6890180, 1037664, 112972, '<td valign="top">Alex, I think this image finished where it deserved to finish.  The main reason for this is she is not separated from the background well enough, especially around the area where the knife is.  What I see on my monitor is a knife held in a hand floating in darkness.  You also need to include some details in her cloths, especially around the knife area because it looks really awkward the way the knife comes off at the viewer.  I had to stare for a long time to figure out the position of her arm and I still can''t tell for sure.  Also, last but not least, the whites in her eyes have been overdone which makes her eyes look unnatural.  I think your score and finish are about right.  Of course, you never complained about your overall finish, I was just trying to give you my feedback :)  Keep up the great work!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2012-10-24 20:35:23.</i></td>', 'Alex, I think this image finished where it deserved to finish.  The main reason for this is she is not separated from the background well enough, especially around the area where the knife is.  What I see on my monitor is a knife held in a hand floating in darkness.  You also need to include some details in her cloths, especially around the knife area because it looks really awkward the way the knife comes off at the viewer.  I had to stare for a long time to figure out the position of her arm and I still can''t tell for sure.  Also, last but not least, the whites in her eyes have been overdone which makes her eyes look unnatural.  I think your score and finish are about right.  Of course, you never complained about your overall finish, I was just trying to give you my feedback :)  Keep up the great work!', '2012-10-24 15:27:46.000000', '2012-10-24 21:35:23.000000', 0),
(6890191, 1037774, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bspurgeon:</b></div><hr/><i> Abby Normal </i></td></tr></table>that should have been the title, even if it''s dnmc</td>', 'Originally posted by bspurgeon: Abby Normal that should have been the title, even if it''s dnmc', '2012-10-24 15:54:23.000000', NULL, 0),
